From 06cc22523227651229a2bee370ade31c9e5172e6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: CoreyKatzburg <64795827+CoreyKatzburg@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 07:47:47 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 07/17] Telemetry: remixShaderCompiles per frame and a
 stuck-compile log line

con_bright_hall (run 20261116-063147) never ray traced: Remix holds ray tracing back
while any Remix pipeline is queued or compiling, and nothing recorded that count.

- rtx_telemetry.jsonl gets remixShaderCompiles (pipelines queued or compiling at frame
  end) from the first frame of the launch, so the loading-screen wait can be told apart
  from a loading screen paced near 30 FPS.
- After 30 s of waiting with ray tracing on, one warning names the oldest compiling
  pipeline and its age with in-flight, compiling, queued and completed counts (one
  compile that never returns vs compiles that keep arriving). Waits of 1 s or more log
  their length when they end.
- dxvk_state_cache/dxvk_pipemanager (NV-DXVK blocks): read-only status of in-flight Remix
  compiles and a completed count. Nothing changes how or when anything compiles.

Amp-Thread-ID: https://ampcode.com/threads/T-01a1e070-32c4-730c-bdfc-76d09e1f79eb
Co-authored-by: Amp <amp@ampcode.com>
